---
description: Rust/core implementation rules for Cryptex
globs:
  - "**/*.rs"
alwaysApply: false
---

For Rust and core-domain work:
- Prefer simple, deterministic and testable implementations.
- Use typed errors and structured diagnostics.
- Do not silently swallow corruption, signature failures or schema incompatibility.
- Keep platform-specific behavior behind platform adapters rather than scattering OS conditionals through domain code.
- Security-sensitive operations belong in the trusted Rust/core boundary where specified.
- Do not implement custom cryptography.
- Preserve canonical/derived storage boundaries defined by the Master Spec and accepted ADRs.
- Add or update tests for behavior changes.
